/* ============================================================================
pascal-row.epher -- the n-th row of Pascal's triangle

The n-th row of Pascal's triangle (Blaise Pascal, 1653; known to earlier
mathematicians) holds the binomial coefficients ncr(n, 0) .. ncr(n, n), and
the row sums to 2^n because it expands (1 + 1)^n. A for loop collects the
nine entries of row 8 into one list; a quiet while loop adds the same
coefficients to check the sum. Everything is exact.

Run it from a terminal:
  Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/algebra/polynomials/pascal-row.epher
  Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\algebra\polynomials\pascal-row.epher"
  macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/algebra/polynomials/pascal-row.epher

The knob to edit is n below.
============================================================================ */

// ---- the knob ----------------------------------------------------------------
const n = 8

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
// row n of Pascal's triangle, k = 0..n
for k in 0 to n do ncr(n, k)
// row sum, added quietly (a for loop would echo all nine partial sums)
s = {0, 0}
while s[1] <= n do s = {s[1] + 1, s[2] + ncr(n, s[1])}
print("row sums to:", s[2])
print("row sum equals 2^n:", s[2] == 2 ^ n)
/* ---- expected output ----
= 8
= {1, 8, 28, 56, 70, 56, 28, 8, 1}
= {0, 0}
= row sums to: 256
= row sum equals 2^n: true
*/
